---
import TopNav from '../../components/TopNav.astro';
import SEO from '../../components/SEO.astro';

const faq = [
	{
		q: "What should I do in 7th grade to prepare for college?",
		a: "Explore — try new clubs, sports, and extracurriculars with an open mind. Give yourself a challenge so you get used to doing hard things early. Quitting counts too — trying five things and keeping two tells you almost as much about yourself as sticking with all five."
	},
	{
		q: "What do people get wrong about 7th grade and college prep?",
		a: "Waiting until 9th grade to start exploring extracurriculars, when 7th grade is actually a better time — there's more time and less pressure than in 9th grade, when there's less time and more pressure to find the activity."
	},
	{
		q: "Does 7th grade count on a college application?",
		a: "No — nothing from 7th grade goes toward a college application. That makes it one of the only times to try things purely because you're curious, not because they'll look good later."
	},
	{
		q: "What tests or deadlines matter in 7th grade?",
		a: "State testing in some districts, but none of it counts toward a college application."
	}
];
const faqSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "FAQPage",
	"mainEntity": faq.map((item) => ({
		"@type": "Question",
		"name": item.q,
		"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": item.a }
	}))
};
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<SEO
		title="7th Grade College Prep: Find Out What You Like — Six Years Out"
		description="7th grade is the year to explore clubs, sports, and interests with nothing on the line — here's how to make the most of it."
		path="/grades/7"
	/>
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,600;9..144,700&family=Inter:wght@400;500&display=swap">
</head>
<body>
<TopNav current="grades" />

<article class="grade-page">
  <header class="grade-head">
    <div class="grade-badge">7</div>
    <span class="eyebrow">Grade 7</span>
    <h1>Find out what you like</h1>
    <p class="lede">Don't be afraid to explore both inside and outside of the classroom.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What to do now</h2>
    <p>Don't be afraid to explore! 7th grade is all about figuring out what you like — try new clubs, sports, and extracurriculars, going into each with an open perspective.</p>
    <p>Give yourself a challenge. High school, and even 8th grade, can be challenging, so if you train your brain to overcome challenges and do hard things early, you're already a step ahead of everyone else. Whether that means doing a hard sport you aren't used to, or entering yourself in a challenging math program after school, you're rewiring your brain in a way that will be incredibly beneficial for you in the future.</p>
    <p>Quitting counts too. It's just as useful to try something and realize it's not for you as it is to stick with something that is — trying five things and keeping two tells you almost as much about yourself as sticking with all five would. Just make sure to keep your commitment.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What most people get wrong</h2>
    <p>Waiting until freshman year to start exploring extracurriculars, when 7th grade is actually a better time to start. This is because there is more time and less pressure in 7th grade versus in 9th grade, when there is less time and more pressure to find the activity. If you start exploring early, by the time you get to high school your foundation will be established and you can build on from there.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What counts</h2>
    <p>Nothing. This year is free to experiment. Enjoy the low stakes of being a kid while it's possible.</p>
    <p>Because nothing now goes toward an application, that means it's one of the only times you'll get to try things purely because you're curious, not because they look good on paper later.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>Tests and deadlines</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>State testing in some districts, but none that will come anywhere near going on your college application</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="related">
    <h2>More resources</h2>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a class="article-card" href="/passion-project">
        <h3>What is a passion project?</h3>
        <p>And how do you find one that's actually yours, instead of one that just looks good on paper?</p>
        <span class="read-more">Read more →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="article-card" href="/good-study-habits">
        <h3>Good study habits</h3>
        <p>What actually works, and how to start building the habit before high school makes it non-negotiable.</p>
        <span class="read-more">Read more →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="grade-nav">
    <a class="back" href="/timeline">← Back to the timeline</a>
    <a class="next" href="/grades/8">Next grade →</a>
  </nav>
</article>

<style>
:root{
  --paper:#FAF4EA;
  --ink:#12283D;
  --ink-soft:#4A5C70;
  --ink-faint:#7A8899;
  --rule:#E4D9C6;
  --g6:#E6F1FB;
  --g7:#B5D4F4;
  --g8:#85B7EB;
  --g9:#378ADD;
  --g10:#185FA5;
  --g11:#0C447C;
  --g12:#042C53;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{
  margin:0;
  background:var(--paper);
  color:var(--ink);
  font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;
  font-size:16px;
  line-height:1.6;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}
.grade-page{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 24px 120px}
.grade-head{text-align:center;margin-bottom:56px}
.grade-badge{
  width:48px;height:48px;margin:0 auto 20px;border-radius:50%;
  background:var(--g7);border:1px solid var(--g8);color:var(--g12);
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:20px;
}
.eyebrow{display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--g10);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;margin-bottom:14px}
.grade-head h1{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:700;font-size:34px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 14px;letter-spacing:-0.01em;text-wrap:balance}
.lede{font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0}

.grade-section{margin-bottom:40px}
.grade-section h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:19px;color:var(--g10);margin:0 0 12px}
.grade-section p{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 12px}
.grade-section p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.grade-section ul{margin:0;padding-left:20px}
.grade-section li{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:8px}
.grade-section li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}

.related{margin-bottom:40px}
.related h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:19px;color:var(--g10);margin:0 0 16px}
.related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));gap:16px}
.article-card{
  display:block;padding:24px;border-radius:14px;
  background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);
}
.article-card:hover{border-color:var(--g10)}
.article-card:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}
.article-card h3{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 10px}
.article-card p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0 0 14px}
.article-card .read-more{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--g10)}

.grade-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:8px}
.back{font-size:14px;color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.back:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.back:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}
.next{font-size:14px;color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.next:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.next:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}

@media (max-width:640px){
  .grade-page{padding:56px 20px 96px}
  .grade-head h1{font-size:28px}
}
</style>
</body>
</html>
